What are Diabetes Drugs?
Diabetes drugs constitute a broad category of pharmaceutical agents specifically designed to manage blood glucose levels in individuals diagnosed with diabetes. This chronic metabolic disorder manifests with characteristic symptoms including frequent urination, persistent thirst, and unexplained weight loss, necessitating lifelong management strategies. The therapeutic arsenal primarily encompasses insulin formulations and a diverse range of oral antidiabetic medications including biguanides, sulfonylureas, thiazolidinediones, and newer classes like GLP-1 receptor agonists and SGLT2 inhibitors, each targeting different physiological pathways involved in glucose regulation.
